1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:01,153
Meet Plate.

2
00:00:01,153 --> 00:00:09,850
Paste your data, and it designs an editorial infographic, rendered by Tencent's Hy Image 3.5 on GMI Cloud.

3
00:00:10,400 --> 00:00:15,543
Pick where it will run and a style, then paste your data and the source.

4
00:00:15,543 --> 00:00:22,400
Meta's Muse Spark 1.3 turns your brief into a design spec, with every word and number locked in.

5
00:00:22,950 --> 00:00:24,970
Hy Image renders it at 2K.

6
00:00:24,970 --> 00:00:31,030
Muse Spark reads it back, blind, and code checks every label against the spec.

7
00:00:31,580 --> 00:00:36,860
On this run, Hy drew a pointer that tied a note about the whole chart to Zambia.

8
00:00:37,410 --> 00:00:41,650
Plate flagged it, and one Hy edit erased just that line.

9
00:00:42,200 --> 00:00:50,280
You get the graphic, checked 31 of 31, with takeaways, a caption, alt text and the data table.

10
00:00:50,830 --> 00:00:54,437
Small print is where image models slip.

11
00:00:54,437 --> 00:01:00,910
On a copper test render, Hy printed a world total of 23,000 as 28,000.

12
00:01:01,460 --> 00:01:03,940
It misspelled Summaries.

13
00:01:04,960 --> 00:01:08,594
And it added axis numbers nobody asked for.

14
00:01:08,594 --> 00:01:10,960
One Hy edit fixed all three.

15
00:01:11,510 --> 00:01:17,510
Copper: Chile mined more than the United States, China and Russia combined.

16
00:01:18,060 --> 00:01:22,860
Coffee: Brazil grows more than the next four countries together.

17
00:01:23,410 --> 00:01:28,450
Cotton: China grew more than Brazil and the United States combined.

18
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:36,760
Lithium: Australia, China and Chile mined nearly three-quarters of world output, not counting the U.S.

19
00:01:37,310 --> 00:01:42,190
Every pixel and every letter, by Hy Image 3.5.

20
00:01:42,740 --> 00:01:43,220
Plate.

21
00:01:43,220 --> 00:01:46,420
The code and prompts are open on GitHub.
